.TH smi-versions-spider "1" "June 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Packages Command"
.SH NAME
smi-versions-spider \- Crawl upstream sources and report the latest download URLs for managed packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-versions-spider
.B \-a
.br
.B smi-versions-spider
.B \-n
.IR NAME [\, ,\fBN\fR\|.\|.\|.]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B smi-versions-spider
drives a headless Firefox browser (via Selenium and GeckoDriver) to visit the
official download or release page of each managed package and print the latest
stable download URL to standard output.
The output can be compared against the corresponding
.I .package
files to identify packages that need updating.
.PP
Each run opens a real browser session; JavaScript-rendered pages are handled
correctly.
EAP, alpha, beta, and release-candidate builds are excluded unless noted.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-all
Crawl all registered packages and print one URL per package.
Packages that fail are reported with a leading
.B ❌
error line; other packages continue.
.TP
.BI \-n\  NAME \fR,\fB\ \-\-name= NAME
Crawl only the named package.
Repeat the option to query multiple packages.
.I NAME
must be one of the registered package names listed below.
.SH PACKAGES
The following package names are registered:
.PP
\fBargo\fP, \fBbazel\fP, \fBchromedriver\fP, \fBclion\fP, \fBcmake\fP,
\fBcm\fP, \fBdagu\fP, \fBelixir\fP, \fBfirefox\fP, \fBforgejo\fP,
\fBfreenginx\fP, \fBgeckodriver\fP, \fBgo\fP, \fBgradle\fP,
\fBgrails\fP, \fBgraphviz\fP, \fBgreenmail\fP, \fBgroovy\fP, \fBh2\fP,
\fBhsqldb\fP, \fBidea\fP, \fBinfinispan\fP, \fBinnosetup\fP,
\fBjanet\fP, \fBjdk\fP, \fBjenkins\fP, \fBjpm\fP, \fBjulia\fP,
\fBkeycloak\fP, \fBlfe\fP, \fBlibreoffice\fP, \fBlibrewolf\fP,
\fBmitmproxy\fP, \fBmvn\fP, \fBmvnd\fP, \fBnetbeans\fP, \fBnginx\fP,
\fBninja\fP, \fBnode\fP, \fBnsis\fP, \fBopenbao\fP, \fBpycharm\fP,
\fBpython\fP, \fBsapling\fP, \fBsbcl\fP, \fBselenium\fP, \fBsolr\fP,
\fBtelegram\fP, \fBthunderbird\fP, \fBtomcat\fP, \fBzookeeper\fP
.PP
Three of them report something other than one binary download URL.
.TP
.B freenginx
has no binary release. The download page carries a mainline table and a stable
table; only the stable one is read, and the URL is the stable source tarball.
The package builds from Mercurial rather than from that tarball, so the version
in the URL is what it needs: its tag is \fBrelease\-\fIversion\fR and follows
from \fBFREENGINX_VERSION\fR.
.TP
.B forgejo
prints two lines, the server binary and the systemd unit, because the package
downloads both.
.TP
.B sapling
prints the Linux x64 archive of the newest release. The release tag carries a
plus sign and the URL shows it percent encoded.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All requested packages were crawled successfully.
.TP
.B 1
One or more packages failed; the failing entries are printed to standard output
prefixed with
.BR ❌ .
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Report the latest version URL for all packages:
.IP
smi-versions-spider \-a
.PP
Report only IntelliJ IDEA, PyCharm, and CLion:
.IP
smi-versions-spider \-n=idea \-n=pycharm \-n=clion
.PP
Report only the latest Maven release:
.IP
smi-versions-spider \-n=mvn
.PP
Report the stable freenginx source tarball, whose version the package builds from:
.IP
smi-versions-spider \-n=freenginx
.SH AUTHOR
.PP
Command written by Imre Tabur.
